  <h2>Build a natural project result and a flexible family chain</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the team made steady progress and met the grant deadline" data-hint="Begin with The team, add made steady progress, then and met the grant deadline." data-fix="The team made steady progress and met the grant deadline." data-success-message="Correct. Make progress reports development, and meet the deadline reports completion by the required time.">
    <h3>Build 1: combine two verb-noun achievements</h3><p class="tile-target">Report progress and timely completion without changing their meanings.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="deadline">deadline</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="team">team</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="progress">progress</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="made">made</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="grant">grant</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="steady">steady</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="The">The</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="and">and</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="met">met</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the successful application provided funding for six practical workshops" data-hint="Begin with The successful application, then provided funding for six practical workshops." data-fix="The successful application provided funding for six practical workshops." data-success-message="Correct. Successful is the adjective, application is the noun subject, and practical modifies the workshop noun.">
    <h3>Build 2: place three family and modifier jobs accurately</h3><p class="tile-target">Describe the request, its result, and the workshop type.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="workshops">workshops</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="application">application</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="six">six</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="funding">funding</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="The">The</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="practical">practical</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="successful">successful</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="provided">provided</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="for">for</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the lexical relationship</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="did" data-hint="Progress is the noun in a conventional partnership with make." data-fix="The team made significant progress on the guide this month." data-why="Make progress is the broadly natural verb-noun collocation; on introduces the project receiving the work." data-success-message="Correct. The repair retrieves make progress and preserves the project relationship with on.">
    <h3>Repair 1: replace the translated verb</h3><p>Tap the verb that does not partner naturally with the noun in this meaning.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="team">The team</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="did">did</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="progress">significant progress</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="month">on the guide this month.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="successfully" data-hint="The word directly before application must describe a noun." data-fix="Their successful application met every published requirement." data-why="Successful is the adjective that modifies application; successfully is an adverb and cannot fill this noun-modifier slot." data-success-message="Correct. The adjective successful now modifies the noun application.">
    <h3>Repair 2: choose the adjective before the noun</h3><p>Tap the family member with the wrong grammatical job.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="their">Their</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="successfully">successfully</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="application">application met</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="requirements">every published requirement.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="clear" data-hint="The word describes how the presenter explained the conclusion." data-fix="The presenter explained the conclusion clearly to the board." data-why="Clearly is the adverb that modifies the action verb explained; clear would describe a noun or follow a linking verb." data-success-message="Correct. The adverb clearly now modifies the manner of explanation.">
    <h3>Repair 3: modify the action, not a noun</h3><p>Tap the adjective where the action requires an adverb.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="presenter">The presenter</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="explained">explained the conclusion</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="clear">clear</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="board">to the board.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build a vocabulary record you can retrieve and adapt</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A useful record is small enough to review and rich enough to use. Start with one core partnership, then add only relationships that solve a real learning problem.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>field</th><th>example for <span class="ex">agreement</span></th><th>purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>core chunk</td><td><span class="ex">reach an agreement on the schedule</span></td><td>stores the verb, article, noun, and topic preposition</td></tr>
      <tr><td>meaning and context</td><td>a shared decision after discussion</td><td>prevents memorizing sound without meaning</td></tr>
      <tr><td>natural alternative</td><td><span class="ex">come to an agreement</span></td><td>adds flexibility without an unranked synonym list</td></tr>
      <tr><td>family or related forms</td><td><span class="ex">agree · agreement · agreeable</span></td><td>connects jobs while preserving distinct meanings</td></tr>
      <tr><td>sound</td><td><span class="ex">aGREE · aGREEment · reach_an_agreement</span></td><td>stores stress and linking with the phrase</td></tr>
      <tr><td>contrast</td><td>not <span class="ex">arrive to an agreement</span> in standard U.S. English</td><td>records the specific repair that matters</td></tr>
      <tr><td>new sentence</td><td><span class="ex">The library and the project reached an agreement on evening access.</span></td><td>proves the learner can adapt the chunk</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to reveal a real job application, rejection, unemployment, performance review, employer, salary, deadline failure, academic result, immigration application, health information, financial difficulty, or private workplace project. Use Westbridge or a tutor-supplied fictional context. The goal is lexical control, not evaluation of the learner’s real success or productivity.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Chunk expansion:</b> Begin with one noun, find two high-value verb partners, and explain how the verbs change the stage or meaning.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Family map:</b> Place four real family members into complete slots, then label action, person, thing or process, description, and manner.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Register test:</b> Give one neutral and one more formal version. Explain which relationship stays the same and what changes in tone.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Retrieval test:</b> Hide the English chunk, use a situation cue instead of a one-word translation, say the phrase, and reuse it in a new sentence.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: deliver a 90-second fictional project-language upgrade</h3>
    <p>Use the Westbridge file or another tutor-supplied fictional project. State the need and research method; report preparation with at least four verb-noun collocations; describe one major issue, one practical solution, and one reliable source or service; transform at least three roots across different grammatical jobs; use one word-plus-preposition partnership; distinguish a neutral and more formal alternative; preserve the evidence limit; recommend a measured next step; and answer one language-coach request by reusing a corrected chunk in a new sentence. Make the stress audible in <span class="ex">deCIDE, deCIsion, apPLY, appliCAtion, make PROgress</span>, and <span class="ex">proGRESS</span>.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener recover each partnership, grammatical slot, exact family meaning, register choice, project fact, evidence limit, and next action without hearing an invented word form, translated collocation, or inflated success claim?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved natural verb-noun partnerships, family jobs, prepositions, legitimate register alternatives, stress, and a retrieval-ready vocabulary record.">
    <h3>Final check: choose the form and partnership the context supports</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The team made steady progress and met the deadline." data-hint="Retrieve make progress and meet a deadline as two different project achievements." data-fix="The team made steady progress and met the deadline."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence uses both verb-noun partnerships naturally?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team made steady progress and met the deadline.">The team made steady progress and met the deadline.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team did steady progress and caught the deadline.">The team did steady progress and caught the deadline.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The deadline progressed the team an agreement.">The deadline progressed the team an agreement.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The applicant submitted a successful application and explained it clearly." data-hint="Use the person noun, adjective-plus-request noun, and adverb after explained." data-fix="The applicant submitted a successful application and explained it clearly."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence places four family or modifier jobs accurately?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The applicant submitted a successful application and explained it clearly.">The applicant submitted a successful application and explained it clearly.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The apply submitted a successfully applicant and explained it clear.">The apply submitted a successfully applicant and explained it clear.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The application successful the applicant clearly.">The application successful the applicant clearly.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The team succeeded in meeting the requirement and took responsibility for the follow-up." data-hint="Succeed takes in plus -ing; responsibility takes for plus a noun." data-fix="The team succeeded in meeting the requirement and took responsibility for the follow-up."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence preserves both word-plus-preposition patterns?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team succeeded in meeting the requirement and took responsibility for the follow-up.">The team succeeded in meeting the requirement and took responsibility for the follow-up.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The team succeeded to the requirement and took responsibility on the follow-up.">The team succeeded to the requirement and took responsibility on the follow-up.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The requirement succeeded the team of responsibility.">The requirement succeeded the team of responsibility.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Do research is neutral; conduct research is more formal, and both can be natural in the right setting." data-hint="Do not turn a register preference into a false grammatical ban." data-fix="Do research is neutral; conduct research is more formal, and both can be natural."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which statement accurately treats a legitimate register alternative?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do research is neutral; conduct research is more formal, and both can be natural in the right setting.">Do research is neutral; conduct research is more formal, and both can be natural in the right setting.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Conduct research is the only grammatical phrase in every conversation.">Conduct research is the only grammatical phrase in every conversation.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do research always means poor-quality research.">Do research always means poor-quality research.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Make PROgress uses the noun; the project will proGRESS uses the verb." data-hint="Use the make-plus-noun frame and will-plus-base-verb frame with their U.S. stress patterns." data-fix="Make PROgress uses the noun; the project will proGRESS uses the verb."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which statement connects stress to grammatical job?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Make PROgress uses the noun; the project will proGRESS uses the verb.">Make PROgress uses the noun; the project will proGRESS uses the verb.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both uses must have verb stress because the spelling is identical.">Both uses must have verb stress because the spelling is identical.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Changing stress turns progress into an adverb of place.">Changing stress turns progress into an adverb of place.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Record a core chunk, meaning, grammar or preposition, family, sound, contrast, and a new contextual sentence." data-hint="Choose the record that supports meaning, form, pronunciation, repair, and later reuse." data-fix="Record a core chunk, meaning, grammar or preposition, family, sound, contrast, and a new contextual sentence."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which vocabulary record is most useful for later retrieval and flexible use?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Record a core chunk, meaning, grammar or preposition, family, sound, contrast, and a new contextual sentence.">Record a core chunk, meaning, grammar or preposition, family, sound, contrast, and a new contextual sentence.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Copy one isolated translation with no phrase, pronunciation, or example.">Copy one isolated translation with no phrase, pronunciation, or example.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Invent every possible suffix without checking whether the forms exist.">Invent every possible suffix without checking whether the forms exist.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect: what information makes a word reusable?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the lexical decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">A collocation differs from a grammar rule because...</span> <span class="ex">Make progress differs from progress as a verb because...</span> <span class="ex">A grammatical slot helps when...</span> <span class="ex">A suffix is only a clue because...</span> <span class="ex">Application differs from applicant because...</span> <span class="ex">Do research and conduct research differ mainly in...</span> <span class="ex">Stress must be stored with each family member because...</span> <span class="ex">A good vocabulary record includes...</span></p>
    <p>Choose one useful noun from an earlier lesson. Build a network with two verb partners, two modifier partners, one preposition if relevant, three real family members, one stress note, one register alternative, one likely learner error, and one new fictional sentence. Remove any item you cannot explain or use.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
  </div>

